hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, meaning Ibn Jafar, Al-Ala narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik bin Anas told him, on the authority of Al-Ala bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H, Bundar told us, Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala. H Abu Musa told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Al-Ala’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. H. Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, Ibn Ulayya told us, on the authority of Ruh bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya'qub, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the cemetery, greeted its people, and said: Peace be upon you, people of the house of a believing people, and we, God willing, will join you. I wish we had seen our brothers.” They said: Have we not? With your brothers, O Messenger of God? He said: “You are my companions, and my brothers are people who have not yet come, and I will leave you at the basin.” They said: How do you know who has not yet come from? Your nation, O Messenger of God? He said: “Do you think that if a man with black horses was riding between the backs of horses with black horses, would he not know his own horses?” They said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: “They will come suddenly, with white hair from the effect of ablution, and I will lead them to the basin, so that men will be pushed away from my basin just as a camel is pushed away.” “The lost one, I call them, ‘Come on,’ and it will be said, ‘They started the story after you.’ And I say, ‘Screw it, screw it.’” This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Ulayya."
